# Revenue Workspace

When editing the customer-centric workspace shell or any lifecycle-tab content, read these for context:

- **`docs/03-customer-workspace.md`** — shell anatomy (customer header, journey rail, record context bar, insight rail, tab gating, list-then-detail pattern, cross-tab linking)
- **`docs/04-lifecycle-tabs.md`** — per-tab specs for Customer / Quote / Contract / Invoicing / Payment / RevRec (sections, context bar fields, Account 360 anchor + lifecycle content, insight rail scope, SLG edge cases)
- **`docs/07-dynamic-status.md`** — how tab statuses, AI insights, next-best-actions, and customer health are derived from mock data
- **`docs/02-design-system.md`** — badge catalog, severity colors, spacing
- **`docs/11-workspace-cleanup-and-gating.md`** — tab gating rules, list-then-detail, use-case matrix

## Key rules

1. All detail routes render through `CustomerRevenueWorkspace` — no standalone pages.
2. Statuses, insights, NBAs are **derived** from mock data via `derive-stage-data.ts` — never hardcoded.
3. Record context bar is hidden on Customer tab, mandatory on all others.
4. Don't gate downstream tabs when an **active prior contract exists** (even if a renewal quote is pending).
5. Revenue recognition is independent of cash receipt.
